ve end.","published":"2026-11-26T21:21:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50606035/sources-de-dj-jacobs-decommits-ohio-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Friday Night Lights,' 'Ted Lasso' top poll ranking 21st-century sports shows","description":"A Seton Hall poll crowns America's favorite modern fictional sports TV series.﻿","published":"2026-11-26T16:01:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50576889/top-fictional-sports-series-21st-century","type":"Story","byline":"Brianna Williams","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"The oldest grudge in football","description":"When Texas Tech and its brash benefactor bought their way into the college football big time, they were settling an old West Texas score.","published":"2026-11-26T13:12:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50427039/texas-tech-puf-cody-campbell","type":"Story","byline":"Dave Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Take a 360-degree look at college football's iconic rivalry trophies","description":"Whether ancient, animal or absurd, college football's rivalry trophies take many shapes.","published":"2026-11-26T13:09:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/id/50371090/college-football-rivalry-trophies","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4916996/ahmad-moten-sr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Moten_Sr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ahmad Moten Sr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Moten_Sr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:13Z","intro":"Ahmad Moten Sr. (born April 22, 2004) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Moten Sr. attended Cardinal Gibbons High School in Fort Lauderdale, Florida. As a senior he had 39 tackles and three sacks. He committed to the University of Miami to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Moten Sr. played in two games and reshirted his first year at Miami in 2022. He played in 11 games and had two tackles with one interception as a redshirt freshman in 2023 and started two of 11 games, recording 18 tackles with one sack as a redshirt sophomore in 2024. Moten Sr. returned to Miami as a starter his redshirt junior year in 2025."}]}}